<p>
<a href="https://social.tchncs.de/@zyzzyxdonta/117387493564517016">David Pape asked:</a>
</p>

<blockquote>
<p>
I just typed
</p>

<p>
<code>&gt;Closes: #47, #48, #49, #50, #51, #52, #53, #54</code>
</p>

<p>
into a commit description, all by hand.
</p>

<p>
Is there a way in Emacs to expand some kind of range description to make this easier? 😅
</p>

<p>
I want to expand strings like "5-10, 15-18, 3" into numbers.
</p>
</blockquote>

<p>
Hmm, could be useful. It reminds me of how page ranges work, which will be handy if I want to tinker with PDFs. Let's see if something like this works:
</p>


<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-emacs-lisp"><code>(<span class="org-keyword">defun</span> <span class="org-function-name">sacha-parse-page-range</span> (s)
  <span class="org-doc">"Parse a page range string and return a list of numbers.</span>
<span class="org-doc">Ex: 1-5</span>
<span class="org-doc">2-4, 6-10</span>
<span class="org-doc">1 4 7-9</span>
<span class="org-doc">3-11/2   - this one specifies an increment"</span>
  (seq-mapcat
   (<span class="org-keyword">lambda</span> (part)
     (<span class="org-keyword">let</span> ((nums (mapcar <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">'</span><span class="org-highlight-quoted-symbol">string-to-number</span> (split-string part <span class="org-string">" *[-/] *"</span>))))
       (<span class="org-keyword">if</span> (= (length nums) 1)
           nums
         (number-sequence (elt nums 0) (elt nums 1) (elt nums 2)))))
   (split-string s <span class="org-string">"[, \t\n\r]+"</span>)))

(<span class="org-keyword">ert-deftest</span> <span class="org-function-name">sacha-parse-page-range</span> ()
  (<span class="org-keyword">should</span> (equal (sacha-parse-page-range <span class="org-string">"5-10"</span>)
                 <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">'</span>(5 6 7 8 9 10)))
  (<span class="org-keyword">should</span> (equal (sacha-parse-page-range <span class="org-string">"1-5, 8"</span>)
                 <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">'</span>(1 2 3 4 5 8)))
  (<span class="org-keyword">should</span> (equal (sacha-parse-page-range <span class="org-string">"1 4 7-9"</span>)
                 <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">'</span>(1 4 7 8 9)))
  (<span class="org-keyword">should</span> (equal (sacha-parse-page-range <span class="org-string">"3-11/2"</span>)
                 <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">'</span>(3 5 7 9 11))))

(<span class="org-keyword">defun</span> <span class="org-function-name">sacha-issue-range</span> (range)
  <span class="org-doc">"Expand RANGE to a list of issues and insert them."</span>
  (<span class="org-keyword">interactive</span> <span class="org-string">"MRange (ex: 1-5, 7): "</span>)
  (<span class="org-keyword">let</span> ((s (mapconcat (<span class="org-keyword">lambda</span> (n) (format <span class="org-string">"#%d"</span> n))
                      (sacha-parse-page-range range)
                      <span class="org-string">", "</span>)))
    (<span class="org-keyword">when</span> (called-interactively-p <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">'</span><span class="org-highlight-quoted-symbol">any</span>)
      (insert s))
    s))
</code></pre>
